    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm looking for some help with a tax question. my family is dealing with an estate that has properties in both the uk and spain, plus some offshore accounts. i need to understand how inheritance tax works when assets are spread out like this and what the main residency rules are for the beneficiaries. thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inheritance tax on a multinational estate is quite complex, as it involves navigating the tax laws of the UK, Spain, and any other jurisdictions where assets are held. You'll need to understand the interaction between UK Inheritance Tax (IHT) and Spanish inheritance tax, which can be a real headache. For beneficiaries, residency rules are crucial because they determine which country's tax laws apply to them, which is a matter of legal domicile, not just where they live for a few months. It's very important to consult with a tax specialist who has expertise in international estate planning.",
      "source": "target",
